2026-07-10 17:53:27,237 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent answered: As a Security and Compliance Officer at Nexus Engineering S.r.l., I can confirm that our company has experience with GDPR compliance, as indicated by the appointment of a Data Protection Officer (DPO) and the availability of a DPA template. Our standard data residency policy is EU only, and we have a cross-border transfer policy that prohibits transfers outside the EU unless there is an explicit legal basis.

To ensure GDPR compliance, we would implement the following security controls: 

We have ISO 27001 certification, which demonstrates our commitment to information security management. The scope of this certification includes the design, development, and operation of AI-powered information systems.

For data protection, we utilize anonymization tools such as Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models. We also have capabilities for implementing data subject rights, including access, rectification, erasure, portability, and objection.

In terms of access control, we enforce multi-factor authentication (MFA) using TOTP and hardware tokens (FIDO2). Role-based access control (RBAC) design is part of our experience, and we have worked with privileged access management (PAM) solutions like CyberArk Conjur and HashiCorp Vault.

Our network security architecture follows zero-trust, micro-segmentation, and defence-in-depth patterns. We also deploy intrusion detection and prevention systems (IDS/IPS) and conduct regular penetration testing.

To guarantee the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of data, we log all queries, ensure log immutability using append-only methods with SHA-256 hash chaining, and retain audit logs for 7 years. We have a security incident response team (SIRT) in place and conduct semi-annual drills to ensure preparedness.

Given these capabilities and our experience with regulatory frameworks like GDPR, we are well-equipped to meet the tender's requirements for strict GDPR compliance, hosting data exclusively within the EU, not transferring data outside the EU, and protecting sensitive data appropriately.
